[Music]  hey everyone welcome to another  installment of harry potter theory today  we're going to be discussing the  hogwarts express and the uk national  rail network  with a platform that's invisible  inaccessible to muggles and a rail line  that heads to a magical school in the  scottish highlands you probably won't be  surprised to hear me say that the  railway trip out to hogwarts is unusual  to say the least  trains play a pivotal part in harry  potter with platform nine and three  quarters and the hogwarts express both  playing a crucial role in harry's first  trip away from the dursleys and off into  the wizarding world  but have you ever wondered how this  magical railway ride fits into a  pre-existing national rail network the  uk national rail network to be specific  does the hogwarts express exist entirely  independently from the rest of these  trains or does it share some of the same  tracks does it transport some of the  same passengers  is the hogwarts express able to  magically avoid collisions what gives  from our perspective it all starts at  platform nine and three quarters at  king's cross station where students  board the hogwarts express a scarlet  steam engine transporting students to  and from hogwarts the platform can be  accessed by walking straight through the  barrier between platforms nine and ten  but you may have a bit of a hard time if  it's a your first go or b you're a  muggle  platform nine and three quarters was of  course filmed at king's tross station on  the edge of central london it's an  active railway station but at the real  station you will find that platforms 9  and 10 are separated by tracks before  filming platforms 4 and 5 were  renumbered 9 and ten and at the station  today you'll find the hidden access to  platform nine and three quarters  complete with half a luggage cart  disappearing into the wall  once you've made it past platform nine  and three quarters next you'll be  boarding the hogwarts express the train  runs between king's cross station and  hogsmeade station making the trip  approximately six times per year or more  if necessary it's on the hogwarts  express that harry's relationship begins  to blossom with the other two members of  the famous trio hermione granger and ron  weasley  once you finish your journey on the  train your next destination as a new  student is a school that you may have  heard of hogwarts school of witchcraft  and wizardry but in order to answer the  question of how this railway network  fits in with the muggle networks we need  to dive deeper into the history of the  hogwarts express  thanks to pottermore we've got some  information that's not particularly well  known even to the bigger harry potter  fans when it occurred to the ministry  that transporting students to hogwarts  needed to be addressed then minister for  magic ottolene gamble came up with a  solution a daring and controversial  solution to the thorny problem of  transporting students was finally  suggested by minister for magic ottolene  gamble who was much intrigued by muggle  inventions and saw the potential in  trains where exactly the hogwarts  express came from has never been  conclusively proven  although it is a fact that there are  secret records at the ministry of magic  detailing a mass operation involving 167  memory charms and the largest ever mass  concealment charm performed in britain  the morning after these alleged crimes a  gleaming scarlet steam engine and  carriages astounded the villagers of  hogsmeade who had also not realized they  had a railway station while several  bemused muggle railway workers downing  crew spent the rest of the year  grappling with the uncomfortable feeling  that they had mislaid something  important  when ottolene gamble commandeered a  muggle train to serve as the new mode of  transport for hogwarts students  she also had constructed a small station  in the wizarding village of hogsmeade a  necessary adjunct to the train  the ministry of magic felt strongly  however that to construct an additional  wizarding station in the middle of  london would stretch even the muggles  notorious determination not to notice  magic when it was exploding in front of  their faces  it was evangeline orpington minister  from 1849 to 1855  who hit upon the solution of adding a  concealed platform at the newly  muggle-built king's cross station which  would be accessible only to witchers and  wizards  with this brief bit of history on the  hogwarts express i suspect that it  either connects onto a muggle train line  shortly after departing from king's  cross or it simply uses its own unique  line the entire way  perhaps even it's a bit of both  to defend point one it would make  perfect sense for witches and wizards to  utilize leverage the existing station's  infrastructure  why construct an entire railway line  when they can simply use what's already  there and cast somewhere in the vicinity  of 167 memory charms to conceal the work  done and achieve said alterations  with this approach all the ministry  would need to do is create a secret  platform then produce some sort of  concealed junction in a location that's  relatively inconspicuous and nearby the  train itself doesn't particularly stick  out or appear inherently magical so  there'd be no reason for them not to use  existing railway lines  as far as collisions with other trains  goes it just so happens that the  hogwarts express underwent several  magical modifications before being  approved by the ministry for school use  i hypothesized that these modifications  were put in place in order to address  this very issue  but i could also be way off the second  point however that the hogwarts express  operates on its own line entirely might  actually make more sense  one of the main pieces of rationale  behind my support for this theory is the  fact that hogsmeade had its own station  built under ottoleen gamble's  instruction a necessary adjunct to the  train  from my perspective there's absolutely  no way that the ministry of magic would  chance a muggle line's arrival in  hogsmeade as that would be a direct  infringement on the international  statute of secrecy which preserves the  divide harmony between muggle and  magical worlds the next argument for  this second theory is that no other  trains are ever mentioned running along  the scenic route of the hogwarts express  it seems as though the hogwarts express  runs along an exceptionally rural route  passing by seemingly very few cities and  towns  the train rattled onwards speeding them  out into open country they made regular  checks on the train as they flew further  and further north each dipped beneath  the cloud showing them a different view  london was soon far behind them replaced  by neat green fields which gave way in  turn to wide purplish moors villagers  with tiny toy churches and the great  city alive with cars like multi-colored  ants  this route provided the omission of  information pertaining to cities is due  to a lack of cities contradicts existing  northern mughal routes out of king's  cross towards scotland that in actuality  passed by many cities and towns  including peterborough durham edinburgh  etc the hogwarts express doesn't appear  to be on any sort of existing rail  network and i say this because no  railway stations are ever mentioned on  its journey with all of that said  perhaps the modifications to the train  by the ministry mentioned earlier were  focused more towards concealment rather  than collision avoidance i'd imagine  that a lone railway line heading towards  a magical school with no stops for that  matter would draw a considerable amount  of attention  to stop any awkward questions it would  be easier to just make the train  invisible to muggle's eyes  cue complex concealment charms  to construct the line which covers a lot  of ground i'd imagine that it would have  taken an awful lot of careful secretive  work  but for dire situations when curious  muggle eyes happened to witness what was  happening there's always the 167 memory  charms mentioned earlier but i do have  one more thing to add in various shots  in the films we see the hogwarts express  traveling across a bridge a bridge that  i happen to know something about  the bridge is known as the glenfinen  viaduct found in scotland it's located  on the west highland line in glenfinan  in vanessa scotland  it is the longest concrete railway  bridge in scotland at 416 yards 380  meters and crosses the river finnen at a  height of a hundred feet  the viaduct also overlooks the glenfenin  monuments and the waters of loxshiel  provided that we have visual proof of  the hogwarts express traveling across a  known bridge and not just random  countryside  evidence would suggest that the hogwarts  express does indeed travel across some  known railway lines  for that reason my final conclusion is  that the hogwarts express travels along  a bit of both  whichever way you break it down  implementing a wizarding transportation  system that's integrated with the muggle  world is no easy feat  the largest ever mass concealment charm  being performed is a testament to just  how seriously this matter was taken and  sometimes i just wonder why not flu  powder  and that's it for this video if you  enjoy the content please like the video  and subscribe to the channel did you  ever wonder about this question  until next time remember  it does not do to dwell on dreams and  forget to live  [Music]

